From b5624db709b5a34fe3870e2859354a15294ba02b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:09:46 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CSV column mapping and add two-level screening analysis

Chapter 6 data editor:
- Map pasted columns by header name (A, B, ..., y) instead of position;
  ignore run-order columns; refuse extra factor columns and factor codes
  other than -1/0/+1 with a clear message.

Two-level factorial engine (chapter 6 and upload solver):
- For incomplete designs, fit the estimable terms as R's lm() does
  (aliased terms dropped) and report sequential (Type I) sums of squares
  with the real residual df in the full-model card.
- Standardized residuals at leverage 1 are NaN, as rstandard(); they are
  left out of the tests (P6.38 now matches R: W = 0.9696, p = 0.8706).
- Reduced model with no selected terms is shown as y ~ 1.

Upload solver:
- New screening route for two-level designs that do not contain every
  treatment combination (Plackett-Burman, fractional factorials), up to
  15 factors: main-effects full model, terms significant at alpha kept in
  the reduced model, then PostHocTest and residual checks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
